ampshire leans slightly Democratic in partisan terms, but Ayotte starts with the advantages of incumbency, high name recognition, and an easy renomination in September.\n\nPolling has been steady all year: every survey shows Ayotte ahead, and the two most recent nonpartisan polls put her lead at four and eleven points among likely voters. Six analysts rate the race between Lean and Safe Republican, and prediction markets give Warmington roughly a one-in-twenty chance. The open question is whether an anti-Trump national environment and an affordability-focused Democratic message can narrow a well-known incumbent's lead in the final weeks.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0651, "margin": -8.09}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0566, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0654, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0669, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0672, "margin": -8.0}]}